  "answer": "In Q3 FY2025, NVIDIA reported a revenue of $35.1 billion, which was significantly higher than the estimated $33.2 billion [Source: earnings-nvda-001], with a growth rate of 93.6% year-over-year (YoY) and an EPS of $0.81 that beat estimates by 9.46% [Source: earnings-nvda-001]. The data center segment contributed $30.8 billion, marking another record quarter for the company [Source: earnings-nvda-001].\n\nFor Q4 FY2025, NVIDIA guided revenue to approximately $37.5 billion (with a range of $37 billion to $38 billion) [Source: guidance-nvda-001], which was above the Street consensus estimate of $37.1 billion at the time of guidance [Source: guidance-nvda-001]. This guidance represented an increase from Q3 FY2025, where they guided revenue to approximately $32.5 billion (with a range of $31.5 billion to $33.5 billion) [Source: guidance-nvda-002], which was slightly above the analyst estimate of $31.7 billion at the time of guidance [Source: guidance-nvda-002].\n\nSources used:\n- earnings-nvda-001\n- earnings-nvda-002\n- guidance-nvda-001\n- guidance-nvda-002",
